  <ym-title|Finite-volume local-pairing proof
  audit><label|finite-volume-local-pairing-proof-audit>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected trace local price estimate.

    <item>Status: draft; independent review requested.

    <item>Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>
    (<verbatim|source/upstream.json>).

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-local-pairing.tex>.

    <item>Scope: prove the finite-volume three-term separation/telescoping
    estimate corresponding to the selected local price bound; isolate the
    exact geometric, probe, and growth receipts on which the application
    depends.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Correspondence><label|correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact declaration and
  path>>|<cell|<strong|Correspondence/status>>>|<row|<cell|Cell root
  seminorm>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Cells.Tiling.rootTest>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/Tiling.lean>>|<cell|Exactly the absolute
  reflected-copy moment raised to reciprocal cell count. Each copy is
  translated and pulled back; odd reflection parity conjugates the
  observable. The manuscript spells this as a level-dependent root
  bound.>>|<row|<cell|Product estimate at two distinct
  sites>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.pulpit>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/HomePort.lean>; its seam input is
  <verbatim|YM.Cells.Seam.inequality>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/Certificate.lean>>|<cell|For
  distinct coarse sites, their fine anchors are distinct; the root bound of
  each observable controls the separated two-site moment. <verbatim|pulpit>
  applies the reflected-cell product inequality to the two anchored
  translates.>>|<row|<cell|Root-bound subadditivity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Cells.Seam.semi>
  and <verbatim|YM.Cells.adds>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/Certificate.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/Chess.lean>>|<cell|The source obtains this by
  expanding the reflected product over all two-color choices and applying the
  positive tiling estimate. It is explicitly an input to the local
  proposition; the article proves the later arithmetic.>>|<row|<cell|Bilinear
  decomposition>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.slides>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/HomePort.lean>>|<cell|Exact
  identity <verbatim|pew(F,H)=pew(f,g)+pew(F,H\<minus\>g)+pew(F\<minus\>f,g)>,
  proved by expanding the integrand and using integrability. The manuscript
  writes and verifies this cancellation directly.>>|<row|<cell|Error
  exponents>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.mileage>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Meteor.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Tau_add>, <verbatim|.tau_mono>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.toll_small>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Arms.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.watch>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Fund.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Gate>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Base.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Tau(P,i,a)=exp((a/10000)(log
  \<beta\>\<#302\>_i)^48)>. Multiplication adds exponents and the function is
  monotone in the exponent. The source growth receipt gives
  <verbatim|4\<leq\>Tau(1)> eventually. The manuscript proves the complete
  chain <verbatim|t\<#207B\>\<twosuperior\>\<#2070\>\<#2070\>+t\<#207B\>\<twosuperior\>\<#2079\>\<#2075\>+t\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>\<#2079\>\<#2075\>+t\<#207B\>\<#2075\>\<#2070\>\<#2070\>\<leq\>4t\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>\<#2079\>\<#2075\>\<leq\>t\<#207B\>\<onesuperior\>\<#2070\>\<#2070\>>.>>|<row|<cell|Measured
  marker root bounds>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.concert>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Traveller.lean>>|<cell|Applies
  <verbatim|journey>, <verbatim|spine_pitch>, <verbatim|open_budget>, and the
  threshold estimate for the rescaling factor to transfer coefficient bounds
  into root bounds. Exact conclusion at grades and sites is the
  <verbatim|t_i(5)> receipt in the chapter. These helper producer bounds are
  not rederived here.>>|<row|<cell|Inserted marker and local
  approximation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.outside>, same
  <verbatim|Traveller.lean>>|<cell|Combines <verbatim|journey>,
  <verbatim|smithies>, <verbatim|capacity_cost>, and <verbatim|open_budget>;
  yields the root bound for the insertion and a bounded local approximation
  in the supported window with root error <verbatim|t_i(\<minus\>300)>. These
  component estimates are remaining source inputs in this
  chapter.>>|<row|<cell|Probe and distant-site
  estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.Probe> and <verbatim|.toll>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Meteor.lean>>|<cell|The probe
  contains a finite-volume approximant in the analytic interior, root
  difference <verbatim|t_i(\<minus\>200)>, and a uniform two-site price
  estimate against every bounded local test in the window. The mission source
  must provide the probe instance.>>|<row|<cell|Actual insertion
  application>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.ear_price>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/PriceLimit.lean>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.small_means>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Terrain.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|ear_price>
  selects the grade-four test, uses mission finances and the finite-volume
  estimate proved in <verbatim|mileage>, then transfers it through the
  separated-site limit. <verbatim|small_means> uses these estimates for each
  test, compatible differentiation, and the selected chart to prove the
  weighted field decay.>>|<row|<cell|Selected response
  route>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Trace.Slate.hullage>, <verbatim|.canal>,
  <verbatim|.legacy>, <verbatim|.rungs>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Phantom.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/Garnet.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|hullage>
  supplies the finite-volume mission for the core-field combination;
  <verbatim|canal> rewrites the response medium using that core field;
  <verbatim|legacy> invokes <verbatim|small_means>; <verbatim|rungs> passes
  the resulting decay to the sensor receipt. The article proves only the
  local finite-volume assembly after its receipts are available.>>>>>

  <section|Proof boundary><label|proof-boundary>

  The proposition in the manuscript is newly organized but follows the exact
  source decomposition <verbatim|slides>, followed by the two reflected-cell
  product bounds <verbatim|pulpit> and the root subadditivity estimate, with
  the same error powers and constants as <verbatim|mileage>. It is a full
  proof of the algebraic and numerical assembly step.

  The following producers are not proved in this chapter:
  <verbatim|concert>'s coefficient-to-root bound, <verbatim|outside>'s
  construction of a bounded local approximation with root error
  <verbatim|\<minus\>300>, the probe's existence and price bound, the finite
  cover/funding estimate used to produce mission finances, and the selected
  chart's derivative/orientation passage from fixed tests to the full field
  norm. They remain explicit inputs, not asserted consequences of the
  proposition.

  <section|Commands and verification record><label|commands-and-verification-record>

  Inspected the exact files listed above using <verbatim|rg -n> and
  <verbatim|sed -n>; read full <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/{Meteor,Traveller,HomePort,Arms,Fund,Base,PriceLimit,Terrain}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Slate/{Phantom,Garnet}.lean>, and
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Cells/{Tiling,Certificate,Chess}.lean>. No Lean or LaTeX
  build was run. No Lean source was modified.

